# Built binaries, anchored to the repo root. Without the leading slash these
# would also match the SOURCE directory cmd/skill-store/, so a new .go file
# added there would be silently unversionable — `git add` would refuse it while
# `git status` stayed clean. The !*.go negation below cannot rescue that: git
# will not re-include a file inside an excluded directory.
/skill-store
/bin/

# Runtime data. The service's SQLite lives under ~/.config/skill-store/, but a
# stray dev copy in the tree should never be committed.
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# Host-local config (machine-specific systemd drop-ins, dev secrets, etc.).
# Put anything that should never leave this machine under ./.local/
/.local/

# Defensive: never accidentally commit credentials.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
id_rsa*
credentials.*
secrets.*

# The globs above target secret *data* files, but they also match source
# (credentials.* once swallowed llm-bridge-server's internal/harness/credentials.go,
# leaving the committed tree unbuildable while `git status` stayed clean).
# Source is never a secret. Files under /.local/ stay ignored — git cannot
# re-include through an excluded directory.
!*.go
!*.sql

# Byte-compiled scorer modules. scripts/sabotage.py is imported by every
# sabotage-*.py plan, so running any scorer writes a .pyc here and leaves the
# tree dirty. One was committed by accident on 2026-08-15; a permanently dirty
# status is read by the next unattended pass as another agent working in this
# repo, which is the one signal it uses to decide not to touch it.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
